title: 'pallet-revive: benchmark some EVM arithmetic op-codes'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-revive` now charges the EVM `DIV`, `SDIV`, `MOD`, `SMOD`, `ADDMOD` and `MULMOD`
    op-codes from their own benchmarks. This change also regenerates all `pallet-revive` weights,
    so the charges of the other EVM op-codes, PVM instructions and host functions change too.

    `pallet_revive::WeightInfo` has 22 new methods, each taking the number of op-codes executed:

    - `evm_pop_opcode`
    - `evm_div_opcode`
    - `evm_div_opcode_one_limb_variant`
    - `evm_div_opcode_mixed_variant`
    - `evm_div_opcode_fixed_knuth_variant`
    - `evm_sdiv_opcode`
    - `evm_sdiv_opcode_one_limb_variant`
    - `evm_sdiv_opcode_mixed_variant`
    - `evm_sdiv_opcode_fixed_knuth_variant`
    - `evm_mod_opcode`
    - `evm_mod_opcode_one_limb_variant`
    - `evm_mod_opcode_mixed_variant`
    - `evm_mod_opcode_fixed_knuth_variant`
    - `evm_smod_opcode`
    - `evm_smod_opcode_one_limb_variant`
    - `evm_smod_opcode_mixed_variant`
    - `evm_smod_opcode_fixed_knuth_variant`
    - `evm_addmod_opcode`
    - `evm_addmod_opcode_one_limb_variant`
    - `evm_addmod_opcode_mixed_variant`
    - `evm_addmod_opcode_fixed_knuth_variant`
    - `evm_mulmod_opcode`

    The arithmetic op-codes are benchmarked in pairs with a `POP`. `DIV`, `SDIV`, `MOD`, `SMOD` and
    `ADDMOD` each have four benchmarks with different operands, and their charge is the largest of
    the four slopes minus the slope of `evm_pop_opcode`. The charge of `MULMOD` is the slope of
    `evm_mulmod_opcode` minus the slope of `evm_pop_opcode`. `POP` itself is charged like the other
    EVM op-codes, not from `evm_pop_opcode`.

    Runtimes that use `pallet_revive::weights::SubstrateWeight` or `()` need no changes. Runtimes
    with their own `WeightInfo` implementation stop compiling until they implement the new methods.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    In EVM contracts, `DIV`, `SDIV`, `MOD`, `SMOD`, `ADDMOD` and `MULMOD` use a different amount
    of gas than before. The regenerated weights also change the gas used by the other EVM
    op-codes, by PVM contracts and by host functions. Results and all other behavior are
    unchanged, and deployed contracts don't need to be redeployed.

    Estimate gas with `eth_estimateGas` instead of reusing gas limits recorded before this change.
    Contracts that pass a fixed gas amount to calls into code that runs these op-codes should check
    that the amount is still enough.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
